ulmonary Disease) and Fibrosis Quística (Cystic Fibrosis), particularly in those who are malnourished. Furthermore, individuals with Anorexia Nerviosa may experience osteopenia due to elevated cortisol levels, which negatively impact bone density. \n\nPreventive measures, such as adequate vitamin D intake, are crucial in mitigating the risk of developing osteopenia. The condition is often seen as a precursor to osteoporosis, highlighting the importance of monitoring bone health in at-risk populations, including those with hyperparathyroidism. Overall, osteopenia represents a multifaceted health issue that requires attention across various medical contexts.\",10\r\n4031,ENFERMEDAD PULMONAR OBSTRUCTIVA CRÓNICA,\"Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease (EPOC), known in Spanish as Enfermedad Pulmonar Obstructiva Crónica, is a progressive lung condition that encompasses diseases such as emphysema and chronic bronchitis. This condition is characterized by obstructed airflow, which leads to difficulties in breathing. EPOC can also be associated with the syndrome of inappropriate antidiuretic hormone secretion (SIADH). Additionally, it is a chronic respiratory illness that requires tailored nutritional interventions, as it can lead to malnutrition and other health complications. Overall, EPOC significantly impacts respiratory function and overall health.\",5\r\n12949,BRONQUIECTASIAS,\"Bronchiectasis, or bronquiectasias, is a medical condition characterized by the abnormal and permanent dilation of the bronchi. This dilation leads to a buildup of mucus, which significantly increases the risk of chronic respiratory infections and other complications. The condition often arises from infections or other lung diseases, and it is associated with chronic inflammation of the airways. As a result, individuals with bronchiectasis may experience not only respiratory issues but also nutritional deficiencies due to the impact on overall health.\",4\r\n12953,EPOC,\"EPOC, or Chronic Obstruc